A||N||5||TSPalmer||Help on Cruise Control||||5||
Z||000000||TSPalmer||03-16-2001||06:58 PM||||Hi everybody! Newbie to both the forum and the world that is Fireo.  I just bought an '85 SE and have been fixing minor things as I have found them (alot with the help of this site).  One prob that has me stumped thus far is the lack of Cruise Control.  Is there any testing I can do to get an idea of what's not happening?  There's nothing on it in the Hayne's or the Chilton's manual at all.  I've searched through the postings on the forum and I noticed a thread that was talking about the switch connected to the clutch (which I'm going to look at right after this), but other than that, I didn't see any info on testing.  Any ideas folks?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">  Thanks, Shawn||||reg||5
Z||000001||Bob Englert||03-16-2001||07:35 PM||||Welcome to the forum.  Great to see more NC Fiero owners.  I sent an email regarding the Tarheel Fieros club.<P>On my original 85 SE, the clutch switch would slip in the braket, causing the switch to be tripped all the time.  This prevented the cruise from working.  I fixed it by installing a small hose clamp in the switch to prevent it from sliding in the braket.<P>The factory manual has detailed troubleshooting info on the cruise system.  There are a lot of things to check in geting the cruise working, including:<BR>- Cruise stalk switch<BR>- Vac leaks in the cruise system (hoses and coffee can)<BR>- clutch and brake cutoff switches<BR>- power to the cruise module<P><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||03-17-2001||10:29 AM||||To which "factory manual" are you referring?  I have a Chilton and a Haynes & also have a copy of the P22.  I need details for my mechanic.  He's checked a few things already, but says that he needs schematics of both the electricals and the vacuum before he can go any farther.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mark||03-17-2001||04:52 PM||||TS,<P>Here's a link to the cruise control diagnostics section of the Fiero On-Line Service Guide. <A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/fierov6/OSG/diag.cruise-control.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nbci.com/fierov6/OSG/diag.cruise-control.html</A> <P>My cruise didn't work in my '86 GT.  Luckily, all that was required was an adjustment of the brake switch. Maybe you too will be so fortunate!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||kiteman||03-17-2001||05:33 PM||||For what it's worth, there's a proximity switch that engages a tab on the brake pedal. When the brake is depressed the switch is opened, and the cruise control is interlocked off.  Mine was not adjusted correctly (body was screwed too far out) and was always open.  Thus no cruise control.  I adjusted it and had all functioning of the cruise control back again.<P>Wish they were all that simple.||||reg||1
Z||000005||TSPalmer||03-18-2001||11:05 AM||||Thanks for all the replies on the cruise problem, I finally got all my honey-do list things (for this weekend) done and now I've got time to go play with the Fiero.  I'll let you folks know what I figure out.  Thanks again, Shawn||||reg||12
